  [PASS] C6b the well-scale response is PROPAGATING, not Jeans-unstable: k(2 pi/r)/k_J = 2 pi/sqrt(2) = 4.44 at EVERY radius (both scales ~ 1/r)   k/k_J = 4.4429 at r_M -- the driven response at galactic scales is the sound branch; the Jeans term does not destabilize (fundamental radial mode marginal, omega^2=0, G081) and does not gap the pole
